# Transient artefacts of `flox lock` / `lock-envs`: a partial lock (`manifest.lock.tmp`) and the
# error it left behind (`.lockerr`). They were tracked once, which is how a FAILED lock came to be
# committed as state — the run that produced them had already been superseded by the next one.
.lockerr
manifest.lock.tmp

# Operator's local re-aim of the flake-input registry. REPLACES the committed
# flake-registry.json when present (see the [hook] in .flox/env/manifest.toml).
# Ignored rather than tracked so a local re-aim never reads as a dirty tree to
# relock's guard rail — which is also why it cannot simply be `git add -f`'ed:
# .gitignore stops protecting a file the moment it is tracked.
#
# ⓘ This is how propagation reaches the catalog from a WORK branch: the committed
# target is branchless, so it resolves rke2lab's default branch — correct when relock
# runs from the trunk, and deliberately wrong from a feature branch, where relock's
# own post-condition says so loudly. Aim this file at the branch instead.
flake-registry.local.json
